Question title:Build Pipeline Directory Tree
Question link:https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/jipp2htnvrww?lecture_hash=v210chxjexei
Solution:

mkdir -p pipeline/stages/build
mkdir -p pipeline/stages/test/unit/integration
mkdir -p pipeline/env/staging
mkdir -p pipeline/env/prod
mkdir -p pipeline/artifacts/old

chmod 750 pipeline/stages
chmod 770 pipeline/artifacts
chmod 700 pipeline/env

cd pipeline/stages/build/
touch app.py config.json NOTES.md
echo "Build stage initialized." > NOTES.md

cd ../..
cd artifacts/old/
touch build.log test.log deploy.log
chmod 640 build.log test.log deploy.log

Approach:
1.i have made the chain of the listed directories using mkdir -p it creates the nested chain of the directories
2.i have given the required permission to that particular directories
3.entered into the given directory and created the files
4.added the text to the NOTES>md
5.returned to the home directory and then entered into other and created *.log files 
6.given permissions to the *.log files